# Never commit real environment values — only *.env.example files should be tracked.
# The broad *.env catches any stray file someone names like "notepad.env" or
# "scratch.env" while working — not just the exact ".env" name — since those
# have held real credentials in the past. It does not affect .env.example
# (that ends in ".example", not ".env").
*.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

node_modules
dist
*.log

.DS_Store

# Runtime generation history (contains customer tile photos and generated
# images). Created on first save; never commit it.
server/data/

# Local working notes from a spec-compliance review. Regenerated on demand and
# specific to one point in time, so it is kept out of the branch history.
AUDIT.md
